course: dictionary
lesson: 11336
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. The word youth can mean a time of life, a group of people, or a feeling.
explain: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults — parents, teachers, youth workers — can help.» Youth workers help young people, so here youth means young people. Ask: what word would fit? Young people fits.
explain: «Songs from someone's youth can bring back strong memories.» Here youth is the time when someone was young. Try the swap: «songs from someone's young years» still makes sense, so that meaning is right.
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning the writer wanted.
fact: Youth means the years between being a child and being an adult.
fact: A youth is a young man or teenager, and the youth means young people as a group.
fact: Youth also means being young: freshness and energy.
fact: Phrases to know: «youth club», «youth team», «youth hostel», «in his youth».
fact: A youth parliament is a group of young people elected to speak for other young people.
exercise: In «Songs from someone's youth can bring back strong memories», what does youth mean? | The youth of today as a group | *The years when someone was young | A teenage boy | A club for sports
exercise: In «trusted adults — youth workers — can help», what does youth mean? | Being full of energy | The time of life of a small child | *Young people | A youth hostel for travellers
exercise: In the news, what does «a youth» usually mean? | *A teenage boy | The time of life when someone is young | A tired old man | A young puppy
test: What is a youth club for? | Cleaning the streets | Old people only | Selling cars | *Young people
test: In «in his youth», what does youth mean? | A group of teenagers | Being a grown-up adult | A holiday hostel | *The time of life when he was young
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Her youth gave her energy and freshness»? | The time when she was a baby | A group of young people as a team | A teenage boy | *Being young, with freshness and energy
